dbr:Kazaam a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "Kazaam"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "Kazaam (/kəˈzæm/) is a 1996 fantasy comedy family film. It was directed by Paul Michael Glaser, written by Christian Ford and Roger Soffer based on a story by Glaser, and starring Shaquille O'Neal as the title character, a 5,000-year-old genie who appears from a magic boombox to grant a 12-year-old boy three wishes. The film was released on July 17, 1996, grossing $19 million on its $20 million budget."@en ;
