dbr:Mediterraneo a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "Mediterraneo"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "Mediterraneo is a 1991 Italian war comedy-drama film directed by Gabriele Salvatores and written by Enzo Monteleone. The film is set during World War II and concerns a group of Italian soldiers who become stranded on a Greek island in the Aegean Sea, and are left behind by the war. It won the Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film in 1992."@en ;
