dbr:Paradise_Lost%3A_The_Child_Murders_at_Robin_Hood_Hills a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "Paradise Lost: The Child Murders at Robin Hood Hills"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "Paradise Lost: The Child Murders at Robin Hood Hills is a 1996 American documentary film directed, produced and edited by Joe Berlinger and Bruce Sinofsky about the trials of the West Memphis Three, three teenage youths accused of the May 1993 murders and sexual mutilation of three prepubescent boys as a part of an alleged satanic ritual in West Memphis, Arkansas. The film uses the music of Metallica instead of an original soundtrack, the first time that the band authorized their music to be used in a film. It was well received by critics, and won the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Informational Programming. It was followed by two sequels, also made by Berlinger and Sinofsky, which followed the evolution of the case through the years: Paradise Lost 2: Revelations in 2000, and Paradise Lost 3: Purgatory in 2011."@en ;
    dbo:director "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Joe_Berlinger_and_Bruce_Sinofsky" ;
